From 6d7762cba3d0b534defe037b5cbc931a5dcf92b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:14:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] macos-arm64: RT flicker fixes

- The view model was drawn after the depth capture, so the layer applied
  the ground's occlusion and reflections to the gun, sliding over it as it
  bobbed. Depth is now captured after the view model and its depth range
  ([0, 0.1] from the engine's depth hack) is left untouched.
- The budget controller switched reflections and AO quality every 30 frames
  when the cost hovered around the budget (which it does at 2560x1440), a
  visible on/off of the lighting. It now needs 60 frames over budget to
  step down, 10 s under budget to step up, remembers what each level cost,
  holds off a level that had to be abandoned soon after it came back, and
  never drops reflections: the last tier traces them at a quarter rate.
- The trace resolution defaults to automatic (rt_divisor 0): half at
  1512x982, a third at 2560x1440, so the cost is similar on any display.
- A frame whose depth resolve has not finished waits for it (rt_fence_wait)
  or reuses the last result instead of dropping the layer for that frame.
- Status line reports frames without a composite and fence misses.
